  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kearney and Company P C obligated $233M in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. Kearney and Company P C received 122 awards with an average award size of $1.9M, and obligations are up 22.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a rise from $158M in FY21 to $233M in FY26, with a peak at $286M in FY24. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $89.4M, followed by the General Services Administration at $64.1M and the Department of Homeland Security at $23.4M. Offices of Certified Public Accountants is the largest NAICS market at $115M, supported by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $65.3M and Other Accounting Services at $36.2M. Contracting patterns show concentration in audit, accounting, and consulting work, with federal procurement dollars concentrated among a handful of agencies and a small set of professional services NAICS codes. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal buyers of Kearney and Company P C?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $89.4M. The General Services Administration follows with $64.1M, and the Department of Homeland Security accounts for $23.4M. Additional buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $19M and the Department of State at $10.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which services and markets drive Kearney and Company P C obligations?",
        "body": "Offices of Certified Public Accountants is the largest NAICS market at $115M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services account for $65.3M, and Other Accounting Services account for $36.2M. Smaller markets include Building Inspection Services at $14.6M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $2.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
